        "title": "Marine Propulsion",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Propulsion answers the question guide [02] set up: resistance demands a force to\novercome it — where does that force come from, and how efficiently? The answer is almost\nalways a screw propeller, driven through a shaft by a prime mover (usually a low-speed\ndiesel). The chain from fuel to forward motion passes through a series of conversions,\neach with losses, and the naval architect's job is to *match* engine, propeller, and hull\nso the whole train runs near its best efficiency."
    },
